{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> For I have already said to your fathers that I will bring you up — this is \"and afterward they shall come out with great substance\" (Genesis 15:14), and \"I Myself will go down with you to Egypt, and I Myself will also surely bring you up\" (Genesis 46:4) — or I have now decreed that this shall be, like \"you shall decree a thing\" (Job 22:28):"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The second Genesis citation in the Hebrew reads (שם מו ד), where שם normally refers back to the immediately preceding citation; here it clearly points to Genesis 46:4, not Genesis 15. The Job reference appears as (איוב כב כה) in the source; the verse that matches the quoted phrase ותגזר אומר is Job 22:28, so the chapter number may reflect a different versification or a copyist error; I have cited 22:28."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:22.011196413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}